<%# locals: (current:) %>
<%# WHERE THE PERSON IS IN THE FIVE STEPS (Shop manual slice 8; the `welcome` screen): the step on
    screen as the page's caps path ("Step 2 of 5"), and the five listed in the left column, the
    current one lit with the column's square. Rendered from each step's page, it writes both slots
    and draws nothing where it is called. The wizard is Home's section, so this replaces Home's column
    for its five pages (`content_for :column`, design-system.md rule 8).

    Text, not links: Back and Next on each page are the way between steps, so a step not reached yet
    is never a link to a page that needs a project nobody has made. A native <ol>, so a screen reader
    hears the count; `aria-current="step"`, the token for a place in a process. %>
<% keys = WelcomeController::STEPS.keys %>
<% content_for :crumbs, "Step #{keys.index(current) + 1} of #{keys.size}" %>
<% content_for :column do %>
  <div class="column-group">
    <h2 class="column-head">Getting started</h2>
    <ol class="welcome-steps">
      <% WelcomeController::STEPS.each_with_index do |(key, label), i| %>
        <%= tag.li class: "column-row", "aria-current": ("step" if key == current) do %>
          <span class="column-row-num"><%= i + 1 %></span><span class="column-row-name"><%= label %></span>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </ol>
  </div>
<% end %>
